{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117407","id":3397553308,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7Kgoyc","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117407","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117407.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117407.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117407","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117407/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117407/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117407/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/fbe8ec42321e5c65ff5bd7acfce81cca607ce219","number":117407,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Unix: kill process group instead of single process","user":{"login":"Gaktan","id":1674095,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzQwOTU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1674095?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaktan","html_url":"https://github.com/Gaktan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaktan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaktan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaktan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaktan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaktan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaktan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaktan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaktan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaktan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes #97429\r\n\r\nI believe this is only an issue with the snap version of Blender. I tested with a standalone version and it's working as expected.\r\n\r\nThis is because the snapcraft version of Blender creates two processes for some reason. `blender` and `blender-wrapper`. I could not find a reason why they do this.\r\nThe pid we get when creating the process is from the `blender-wrapper`. Killing this process does not kill the `blender` processm which is the one actually running the server and communicating with godot. Not killing the server has unintended consequences, such as the blender python script not able to create the server due to the port already being used, or godot communicating with the wrong server and blocking the entire process.\r\n\r\nThe fix is to kill the entire process group (with negative pid) instead of the single process.\r\n\r\nThis might not be the proper way to handle this issue. It works in the case of Blender, it might have side effects for other scenarios. I can't see why we would want to kill a process but not its children at first glance\r\n\r\nIt might be safer to add a boolean when calling OS::kill(), but I didn't feel like changing the API and implementing the change on windows (far more annoying to implement). \r\nAnother way would be to ask the Blender team to only use a single process in snap package, or ask them to handle process signals for child processes. But I assume they do it for a reason.","labels":[{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-03-13T23:51:44Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T04:28:45Z","closed_at":"2026-03-14T00:57:34Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"df10fe09fb4940658f6d3aafc77e93426fe8526b","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"Gaktan:fix-blender-kill","ref":"fix-blender-kill","repo":{"id":786256936,"nod